{"uid":"267c3fd28f478cce","name":"test_budget_exhausted_with_all_tasks_completed_holds_exhausted","fullName":"tests.test_e2e#test_budget_exhausted_with_all_tasks_completed_holds_exhausted","historyId":"23343602d38e0af363879d31a0e0ffdb","time":{"start":1791921655789,"stop":1791921657626,"duration":1837},"description":"Task 015 (requirement E.1, #169), inverting the old `test_grace_\n    review_when_budget_exhausts_with_all_tasks_completed`/`test_grace_\n    review_not_granted_twice_and_can_fail`: budget sized so the worker\n    iteration that completes the LAST task is also the iteration that\n    exhausts the budget (planning=1, worker=2, worker=3 == the whole\n    3-iteration budget). The off-budget grace review this used to grant\n    is gone -- the run now holds `exhausted`/`verdict: null` through the\n    same plain out-of-budget path C.1 (task 011) established, with no\n    review iteration ever dispatched, REGARDLESS of what the stub review\n    would have said -- proved by running the exact same budget/task shape\n    with `STUB_REVIEW_FAILS` both unset and set and observing the SAME\n    outcome either way, which is the surviving cover for both retired\n    tests.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 015 (requirement E.1, #169), inverting the old <code>test_grace_ review_when_budget_exhausts_with_all_tasks_completed</code>/<code>test_grace_ review_not_granted_twice_and_can_fail</code>: budget sized so the worker<br />\niteration that completes the LAST task is also the iteration that<br />\nexhausts the budget (planning=1, worker=2, worker=3 == the whole<br />\n3-iteration budget). The off-budget grace review this used to grant<br />\nis gone -- the run now holds <code>exhausted</code>/<code>verdict: null</code> through the<br />\nsame plain out-of-budget path C.1 (task 011) established, with no<br />\nreview iteration ever dispatched, REGARDLESS of what the stub review<br />\nwould have said -- proved by running the exact same budget/task shape<br />\nwith <code>STU